<dotnetnuke type="Package" version="5.0">
  <packages>
    <package name="MegaForm" type="Module" version="02.00.021">
      <friendlyName>MegaForm</friendlyName>
      <description>Dynamic Form Builder Module for DNN - drag-and-drop builder, conditional logic, webhooks, anti-spam, email notifications, workflows, Save and Continue, Row/Column layout.</description>
      <iconFile>~/DesktopModules/MegaForm/Images/module-icon.png</iconFile>
      <owner>
        <name>MegaForm</name>
        <organization>MegaForm</organization>
        <url>https://megaform.example.com</url>
        <email>support@megaform.example.com</email>
      </owner>
      <license src="License.txt"/>
      <releaseNotes src="ReleaseNotes.txt"/>
      <azureCompatible>true</azureCompatible>
      <dependencies>
        <dependency type="CoreVersion">09.04.00</dependency>
        <!-- [PersonaBarMerge 2026-08-01] The Content > MegaForm panel used to ship as a separate
             MegaForm.PersonaBar package; it is now part of this one so a site gets the module and
             its admin panel from a single install. The <component type="PersonaBarMenu"> below is
             installed by Dnn.PersonaBar.UI, NOT by DotNetNuke.dll â€” without this dependency the
             component is skipped SILENTLY and the extension installs with no menu entry. -->
        <dependency type="ManagedPackage" version="01.00.00">Dnn.PersonaBar.UI</dependency>
      </dependencies>
      <components>
        <!-- ============================================================
             [AzureResidue 2026-08-11] Delete the Azure DLLs that MegaForm packages built before
             2026-07-26 dropped into bin. The code that used them is long gone (see
             [AzureBlobRemoved v20260726] in the Assembly component below), but a DNN install
             never deletes a bin DLL, so on every site that ever ran an older build the three
             files just sit there — and they are not inert. Azure.Core 1.55 carries an
             assembly-level custom attribute whose type lives in System.ClientModel, which we do
             not ship; DNN attribute-scans EVERY assembly in bin at startup (MEF
             SafeDirectoryCatalog inside ExtensionPointManager), so the scan throws and
             ExtensionPointManager stays faulted for the life of the app domain. Every Control Bar
             / Edit Bar request then returns 500: the administrator cannot enter Edit mode or add
             a module to a page, and on some skins the failure reaches the front end as a
             site-wide 500. Measured on two infected sites: removing exactly these three files
             took ToggleUserMode from 500 back to 405, the same answer a healthy site gives.

             All three must go together. Azure.Storage.Blobs and Azure.Storage.Common reference
             Azure.Core, so deleting Azure.Core alone leaves the scan failing on the survivors.

             Deliberately NOT listed: Dnn.AzureConnector.dll is DNN's own and rides on the older
             Microsoft.WindowsAzure.Storage 9.3.2, an unrelated assembly. And the stale
             MegaForm.Integrations.CloudStorage.dll may still reference Azure — harmless, because
             DnnServiceLocator asks for the S3 type by name through
             Type.GetType(throwOnError: false), so the dead Azure reference is never resolved.

             Cleanup runs only when this version is newer than the installed one, which is why
             the package version moved to 02.00.016 in the same edit. A file that is not there is
             skipped, so this is safe on a clean install.
             ============================================================ -->
        <component type="Cleanup" version="02.00.016" fileName="02.00.016.txt" />
        <!-- ============================================================
             [LocaleSwap 2026-08-13] vi-VN and ru-RU left the shipped locale set.

             A DNN module install EXTRACTS over DesktopModules\MegaForm — it never deletes
             files the new version dropped — and I18nController builds its list by SCANNING
             the i18n folders. Without this cleanup an upgraded site keeps offering Vietnamese
             and Russian in the language picker, so the removal looks like it did nothing.

             A file that is not there is skipped, so this is safe on a clean install.
             ============================================================ -->
        <component type="Cleanup" version="02.00.017" fileName="02.00.017.txt" />
        <component type="Module">
          <desktopModule>
            <moduleName>MegaForm</moduleName>
            <foldername>MegaForm</foldername>
            <businessControllerClass>MegaForm.DNN.Components.FeatureController, MegaForm.DNN</businessControllerClass>
            <supportedFeatures>
              <supportedFeature type="Portable"/>
              <supportedFeature type="Upgradeable"/>
            </supportedFeatures>
            <moduleDefinitions>
              <moduleDefinition>
                <friendlyName>MegaForm</friendlyName>
                <defaultCacheTime>0</defaultCacheTime>
                <moduleControls>
                  <moduleControl>
                    <controlKey/>
                    <controlSrc>DesktopModules/MegaForm/Views/FormView.ascx</controlSrc>
                    <supportsPartialRendering>False</supportsPartialRendering>
                    <controlTitle>MegaForm</controlTitle>
                    <controlType>View</controlType>
                    <helpUrl/>
                  </moduleControl>
                  <moduleControl>
                    <controlKey>Edit</controlKey>
                    <controlSrc>DesktopModules/MegaForm/Views/FormEdit.ascx</controlSrc>
                    <supportsPartialRendering>False</supportsPartialRendering>
                    <controlTitle>Form Builder</controlTitle>
                    <controlType>Edit</controlType>
                  </moduleControl>
                  <moduleControl>
                    <controlKey>Submissions</controlKey>
                    <controlSrc>DesktopModules/MegaForm/Views/Submissions.ascx</controlSrc>
                    <supportsPartialRendering>False</supportsPartialRendering>
                    <controlTitle>View Submissions</controlTitle>
                    <controlType>Edit</controlType>
                  </moduleControl>
                  <moduleControl>
                    <controlKey>Tasks</controlKey>
                    <controlSrc>DesktopModules/MegaForm/Views/Tasks.ascx</controlSrc>
                    <supportsPartialRendering>False</supportsPartialRendering>
                    <controlTitle>Workflow Inbox</controlTitle>
                    <controlType>View</controlType>
                  </moduleControl>
                  <moduleControl>
                    <controlKey>ManageModule</controlKey>
                    <controlSrc>DesktopModules/MegaForm/Views/ManageModule.ascx</controlSrc>
                    <supportsPartialRendering>False</supportsPartialRendering>
                    <controlTitle>Manage module</controlTitle>
                    <controlType>Edit</controlType>
                  </moduleControl>
                  <moduleControl>
                    <controlKey>Settings</controlKey>
                    <controlSrc>DesktopModules/MegaForm/Views/Settings.ascx</controlSrc>
                    <supportsPartialRendering>False</supportsPartialRendering>
                    <controlTitle>MegaForm Settings</controlTitle>
                    <controlType>Admin</controlType>
                  </moduleControl>
                  <moduleControl>
                    <controlKey>FormList</controlKey>
                    <controlSrc>DesktopModules/MegaForm/Views/FormList.ascx</controlSrc>
                    <supportsPartialRendering>False</supportsPartialRendering>
                    <controlTitle>My Forms</controlTitle>
                    <controlType>Edit</controlType>
                  </moduleControl>
                </moduleControls>
              </moduleDefinition>
            </moduleDefinitions>
          </desktopModule>
        </component>
        <component type="Script">
          <scripts>
            <script type="Install">
              <path>SqlScripts</path>
              <name>01.06.42.SqlDataProvider</name>
              <version>01.06.42</version>
            </script>
            <script type="Install">
              <path>SqlScripts</path>
              <name>02.00.018.SqlDataProvider</name>
              <version>02.00.018</version>
            </script>
            <script type="UnInstall">
              <path>SqlScripts</path>
              <name>Uninstall.SqlDataProvider</name>
              <version>01.07.99</version>
            </script>
          </scripts>
        </component>
        <component type="Assembly">
          <assemblies>
            <assembly>
              <name>MegaForm.DNN.dll</name>
              <path>bin</path>
            </assembly>
            <assembly>
              <name>MegaForm.Core.dll</name>
              <path>bin</path>
            </assembly>
            <!-- [2026-06-23] MegaForm.Sdk.dll was missing from the manifest, so every
                 DNN install/upgrade shipped without it. DnnServiceLocator..ctor() loads
                 the SDK, so the FIRST code to touch DnnServiceLocator.Instance (FormsOverview,
                 Reports/Backfill, scheduler tasks like BlogScheduledPublishTask) threw
                 "Could not load file or assembly 'MegaForm.Sdk'". Bundling it here fixes
                 the gap at the source. -->
            <assembly>
              <name>MegaForm.Sdk.dll</name>
              <path>bin</path>
            </assembly>
            <!-- [CloudStorage v20260723-01] Cloud file mirror: Google Drive rides on MegaForm.Core
                 + the framework HttpClient, so it needs no assembly of its own.
                 [AzureBlobRemoved v20260726] Azure Blob provider DROPPED. Azure.Storage.Blobs pulled
                 Azure.Core 1.55 â†’ System.ClientModel + .NET 10 System.* transitively; Azure.Core has an
                 assembly-level attribute whose type lives in System.ClientModel, and DNN scans EVERY
                 bin assembly's attributes at startup (MEF SafeDirectoryCatalog) â†’ a missing
                 System.ClientModel.dll crashed the WHOLE site (TypeInitializationException).
                 [S3AddOn 2026-07-28] Amazon S3 moved OUT of this package into
                 MegaForm.CloudStorageS3_<version>_Install.zip: MegaForm.Integrations.CloudStorage.dll
                 + AWSSDK.Core + AWSSDK.S3 are 0.73 MB that only an S3-mirroring install executes.
                 DnnServiceLocator resolves the provider by reflection, so the module works with or
                 without the add-on and the two can be installed in either order. -->
            <!-- [ScriptingBundled 2026-08-14] After-Submit C# Script engine, +12 MB, bundled on the
                 owner's call. Before this the engine shipped in NO package: every site installed
                 from the zip hit the fail-closed branch "Script compiler is not installed on this
                 server", and the capability had only ever run where these DLLs were hand-copied.

                 ONLY these three Roslyn pieces are shipped. Roslyn 4.10's net472 output is 17
                 assemblies / 18 MB, but a stock DNN 10.3 bin already carries ten of them
                 (System.Collections.Immutable, System.Memory, System.Buffers, System.Numerics.Vectors,
                 System.Runtime.CompilerServices.Unsafe, System.Threading.Tasks.Extensions,
                 System.ValueTuple, System.Text.Encoding.CodePages, System.Text.Json, Newtonsoft.Json)
                 at NEWER versions. Shipping our older copies over DNN's would repeat the Azure
                 mistake described above: DNN scans every bin assembly at startup, and a downgraded
                 framework assembly is how a site loses its Control Bar for the life of the app
                 domain. Verified absent from DNN 10.3.0 (megaclean008) before choosing this set. -->
            <assembly>
              <name>MegaForm.Scripting.dll</name>
              <path>bin</path>
            </assembly>
            <assembly>
              <name>Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.dll</name>
              <path>bin</path>
            </assembly>
            <assembly>
              <name>Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.dll</name>
              <path>bin</path>
            </assembly>
            <assembly>
              <name>System.Reflection.Metadata.dll</name>
              <path>bin</path>
            </assembly>
          </assemblies>
        </component>
        <component type="ResourceFile">
          <resourceFiles>
            <basePath>DesktopModules/MegaForm</basePath>
            <resourceFile>
              <name>Resources.zip</name>
            </resourceFile>
          </resourceFiles>
        </component>
        <component type="File">
          <files>
            <file><name>icon.gif</name></file>
          </files>
        </component>

        <!-- ============================================================
             [PersonaBarMerge 2026-08-01] Content > MegaForm panel.
             Was the separate MegaForm.PersonaBar package (01.00.000); folded in here so one
             install gives a site both the module and its portal-wide admin panel.

             PersonaBar.zip carries the panel's SPA and unpacks into the Persona Bar's own
             Modules folder â€” that path is fixed by the loader, which resolves
             Modules/<folderName>/<path>.{html,js,css} from the menu row below.
             ============================================================ -->
        <component type="ResourceFile">
          <resourceFiles>
            <basePath>DesktopModules/admin/Dnn.PersonaBar/Modules</basePath>
            <resourceFile>
              <name>PersonaBar.zip</name>
            </resourceFile>
          </resourceFiles>
        </component>
        <component type="Assembly">
          <assemblies>
            <!-- net48, unlike MegaForm.DNN.dll (net472): Dnn.PersonaBar.Library on DNN 10.x is
                 built for 4.8 and a 4.7.2 build cannot even reference it. Both load fine on the
                 4.8 runtime every DNN 9.4+ site already requires. -->
            <assembly>
              <name>MegaForm.PersonaBar.dll</name>
              <path>bin</path>
            </assembly>
          </assemblies>
        </component>
        <component type="PersonaBarMenu">
          <menu>
            <!-- identifier is what [MenuPermission(MenuName = "MegaForm")] checks; folderName +
                 path are what the loader turns into Modules/MegaForm/{path}.{html,js,css}.
                 Keep the dated path when changing PersonaBar JS/CSS so RequireJS does not
                 reuse a stale browser-side module keyed by the old path. -->
            <identifier>MegaForm</identifier>
            <moduleName>MegaForm</moduleName>
            <folderName>MegaForm</folderName>
            <resourceKey>nav_MegaForm</resourceKey>
            <path>MegaForm_20260810_F550</path>
            <parent>Content</parent>
            <order>25</order>
            <defaultPermissions>Administrators</defaultPermissions>
          </menu>
        </component>
      </components>
    </package>
  </packages>
</dotnetnuke>

